<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marzuban ibn Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 957</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marzuban ibn Muhammad was a Daylamite ruler of the Sallarid, or Musafirid, dynasty who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> in 941 after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sajid-dynasty">Sajids</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardabil">Ardabil</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and extending his authority over Arran, Shirvan and Armenian princes. He faced a Rus raid that captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Barda'a</a> in 943. Captured by the Buyid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rukn-al-dawla">Rukn al-Dawla</a> in 948, he was imprisoned for several years and regained power before his death in 957.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marzuban-ibn-muhammad.jpg" alt="Marzuban ibn Muhammad" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Interfase · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silver_dirham_of_Marzban_bin_Muhammad_of_Salarids.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
